{"id":"atlas-intro","type":"text","x":0,"y":0,"width":3600,"height":200,"text":"**Engine and scheduling / NOS · 1.43-B**\n\n38 system members · 14 one-hop ghost neighbours · 52 canonical edges\nEvery incoming and outgoing edge of a member is shown, including parallel edges. Ghost cards retain status text and gap badges; grey borders mark neighbours unless a high/critical gap requires red. Arrows retain source direction; MISSING means an absent connection, not working data flow.\nCyan data · orange control · green persist · purple schedule · yellow UI · red event.\n[[NOS System Map.canvas|Return to overview]]","color":"5"},
{"id":"ext-host-tools","type":"text","x":5064,"y":396,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Host tools (flash_watch, sdsync, exports)**\nPython tools: checked flash helper…\n\nruns: Off-watch. Run by the developer on demand.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|1 gap]]\n[[Followup 5 - USB command to handler map and host protocol edge cases|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"hw-button","type":"text","x":4836,"y":1136,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**BOOT button (GPIO0)**\nSide button on GPIO0. ISR with 25 ms…\n\nruns: ISR on edge. Works in every display state.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Power and battery|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"hw-co5300-panel","type":"text","x":5292,"y":1136,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**AMOLED panel 466x466 (CO5300 profile, QSPI)**\n466x466 RGB565 AMOLED on QSPI (CS9, CLK10,…\n\nruns: Hardware. Driven by the flush task; DISPOFF/SLPIN in sleep states.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Hardware and drivers|Open note]]\n↗ GHOST · one-hop neighbour","color":"#808890"},
{"id":"drv-display","type":"text","x":4836,"y":1876,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Display flush and QSPI panel driver**\nStripe job queue to the flush task,…\n\nruns: Jobs queued by the UI task; executed on the flush task (core 1).\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"drv-display-te","type":"text","x":5292,"y":1876,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Display TE wait (no TE on B)**\nTearing-effect synchronisation helper. B…\n\nruns: Never active on B.\n\n`STUB`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"1"},
{"id":"task-asset-read","type":"text","x":4152,"y":2616,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**asset-read task**\nReads asset files from SD off the UI thread…\n\nruns: prio 1. On demand from the orrery card poll.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"timer-pace","type":"text","x":4608,"y":2616,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**pace esp_timer (frame pacing)**\nReleases a semaphore at the frame period so…\n\nruns: esp_timer, 1/fps_cap. Running only while the display is ON.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"task-ui","type":"text","x":5064,"y":2616,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**main / app_main UI loop**\nBoot, power-state machine, serial command…\n\nruns: core 0, prio 1, 8192 B. ON about 60 Hz (40 Hz authored); AOD/SENSOR 1 Hz frames; OFF 50 Hz loop, no frames.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|3 gaps]]\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"task-flush","type":"text","x":5520,"y":2616,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**flush task**\nTakes 16-row stripe jobs, rotates them CCW…\n\nruns: core 1, prio 4, 3 KB, queue depth 3. Per dirty stripe; idle when nothing changes.\n\n`WORKING` · ⚠ [[Gaps|2 gaps]]\n[[Rendering pipeline|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"task-dotbake","type":"text","x":5976,"y":2616,"width":400,"height":296,"text":"**dotbake task**\nBoot-time prebake of dot-matrix masks and…\n\nruns: core 1, prio 1, 3 KB. Boot only.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Followup 4 - Uncovered built files- blur pipeline, orrery shade, fonts|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
{"id":"eng-input","type":"text","x":48,"y":3380,"width":400,"height":272,"text":"**Input recogniser and router**\nTurns touch points and button edges into…\n\nruns: UI task, every frame.\n\n`WORKING`\n[[Engine and scheduling|Open note]]\n● SYSTEM MEMBER","color":"4"},
